{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1295536-making-a-4th-force","id":1295536,"title":"Making a 4th Force?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-10T04:54:08-07:00","id":1295536,"title":"Making a 4th Force?","content":"So the way I see it Quantum is like the Wellspring of Universe. It is the substrata from which new universes may be formed.<br /> <br /> Psi however seems to represent mastery of the fundamental forces, psychics seem to master the facets of reality as is, whether thought, space, kinetic force, energy ect. Mastering it allows you to ascend to the subtle realms beyond this reality.<br /> <br /> And Flux is the power of tapping into the Other. It is the power of the inbetween of the Multiverse summoning potential and causality and probability. Mastering it involves ascending into a new perspective of Reality, so being one with time (past/present/future/maybes)<br /> <br /> So what about the idea of Quantum Gods, or a combination of Quantum Psi and Flux Ascended Beings creating another force, like a 4th or even 5th Force.<br /> <br /> Even with it not being Canon I can see myself using the idea for homebrew games.<br /> <br /> So with Flux we can access alternate reality\u2019s, worlds that use different rules and different Forces. So say a Flux God Creates the concept of the other/elsewhere/beyond, creating essentially a \u201ccheat Potential\u201d. Then Quantum Gods create a Universe if Power, new rules and fundamental Forces. Then Psi gods in Coordination with the Quantum gods anchors a method to tap into this otherforce, maybe it\u2019s a tool like the Green Lantern Rings, or a backside code in our universe such as magical rituals and strange geometries which seems like magic. Or maybe it\u2019s by physically merging the force into a being of this world, like The Flash and the Speed Force, Captain Marvel and Shazam, the Silver Surfer and the Power Cosmic or Jean Grey and the Phoenix.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is just a thought exercise. You could use it to make one off phenomena or mysteries. Or a Unique impossible being. Or more fun to introduce new potential into the setting. Beings that don\u2019t fit the solid stone rules of the Universe.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts? These are just the most ambiguous abstract explanations of events. For instance maybe a wish Force is made so that Ascended Beings could exert their influence in the Universe they left behind, for good or ill and without disrupting the Universal balance of Quantum and Psi.<br /> <br /> Maybe it\u2019s for making a singular Godbeibg who can exist in the Universe like a Celestial or Galactus. Or maybe you can use it to make an otherworldly Force to explain weaker but more omnipresent phenomena like Ritualists or Sorcerers, or even the strange Infrastructure of the Machine God.<br /> <br /> Or even making Exalts in Trinity. Or Mages, both styles. So Ascension mages have Avatars which are these shards of the \u201cOther\u201d which translates belief and will into change. While Awakening Mages Tap into the Supernal, a reality of Truths which you can call upon to change reality.<br /> <br /> Again this can be simplified by just saying a Single Quantum Being Created this Power, like Franklin Richards Creating another World, or it can be As complex as you want to cheat the universe.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T09:59:37-07:00","id":1295576,"title":"","content":"Honestly? I have a bunch of notes on adding Fate/Legend as the fourth force, bringing Scions, Denizens and Sorcerers into certain iterations of the setting. Adventure (1930s) in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T18:19:03-07:00","id":1295705,"title":"","content":"I was tempted to do something like this with Fate as that 4th force to bring all of these Storypath games into one single Continuum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T23:07:09-07:00","id":1295744,"title":"","content":"<i>All</i> of the Storypath games? I'll give Dystopia Rising: Evolution a pass, as it's a licensed product. But there's also They Came From Beneath the Sea, where the \u201cforce\u201d is literally Fourth Wall manipulation.<br /> <br /> Put another way, TCFBtS does what I wish TC had done with Talents: is not probability manipulation or anything else in-universe; is just genre conventions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-11-2019, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T12:06:49-07:00","id":1295889,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I like the fact that talents have an in Universe explanation for their abilities. Additionally I have to say I'm not a huge fan of fate and destiny being a force with mechanical elements to it. (For example I really don't like the fatebinding and such elements of Scion, don't like it at all. So I'm glad it's not in Trinity.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T13:00:17-07:00","id":1295913,"title":"","content":"I like fatebinding, it adds some complexity to the relationships, and, somehow, there is a little bit of it on TC. The way relationships works and allows the characters to do stuff is a big pluss, and it is the base for fatebinding.<br /> <br /> But fate is a divine thing, we need it to keep the gods on their places, otherwise they would be around like the Novas are on Aberrant.<br /> <br /> About legend and fate being added as power sources in TC, no, at least not in the core universe. It would brake the balance between Novas and baselines.<br /> <br /> You can, of course, combine all them to build a Marvel / DC world, and add gods, magic, psionics, aliens, ring bearers (not the halfling kind) and extra dimensional demons, what ever you want to use, but it turns the entire setting in a big mess, like Marvel and DC universe are. MCU and Ultimate Marvel were more \u201cbalanced\u201d focusing more or less on tech, genetic manipulation, mutants and crazy people with a combination of those, and less on the more supernatural (until the ultimate Thor show up from the rainbow... it was bad...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"